# <type>(<scope>): <subject> (Max 50 chars)
# |<----  Using a maximum of 50 characters  ---->|

# Explain why this change is being made
# |<----   Try to limit each line to 72 characters   ---->|

# Provide links or keys to any relevant tickets, articles or resources
# Example: Closes #23

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be:
#   feat     - New feature
#   fix      - Bug fix
#   docs     - Documentation changes
#   style    - Formatting, missing semicolons, etc; no code change
#   refactor - Refactoring code without changing functionality
#   perf     - Performance improvements
#   test     - Adding or updating tests
#   chore    - Maintenance tasks, dependency updates
#   revert   - Reverting a previous commit
#
# Scope is optional and can be anything specifying the place of the commit change.
# Examples: ui, api, auth, components, hooks, etc.
#
# Subject should use imperative mood: "change" not "changed" nor "changes"
# Don't capitalize first letter
# No period at the end
#
# Body should explain the motivation for the change and contrast with previous behavior
#
# Footer should contain any breaking changes or closing issues
# Breaking changes should start with "BREAKING CHANGE:"
# Closing issues should be listed as "Closes #123, #456"
# --------------------